coi me BPFK

Below are the formal definitions of the {l=E2=80=A2i}/{l=E2=80=A2'i} gadri,=
 as they can=20
be found on the BPFK gadri page=20
<http://www.lojban.org/tiki/BPFK+Section:+gadri>:

loi [PA] broda      lo gunma be lo [PA] broda
lei [PA] broda      lo gunma be le [PA] broda
lai [PA] broda      lo gunma be la [PA] broda
loi PA sumti        lo gunma be lo PA /sumti/
lei PA sumti        lo gunma be le PA /sumti/
lai PA sumti        lo gunma be la PA /sumti/

lo'i [PA] broda     lo selcmi be lo [PA] broda
le'i [PA] broda     lo selcmi be le [PA] broda
la'i [PA] broda     lo selcmi be la [PA] broda
lo'i PA sumti       lo selcmi be lo PA /sumti/
le'i PA sumti       lo selcmi be le PA /sumti/
la'i PA sumti       lo selcmi be la PA /sumti/



Now, here is a quote from "gadri: an unofficial commentary from a=20
logical point of view", section 3=20
<http://www.lojban.org/tiki/gadri%3A+an+unofficial+commentary+from+a+logica=
l+point+of+view#Definition_of_gadri>:

According to jbovlaste <http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/selcmi>,=20
{selcmi} is defined as follows:

x1 selcmi x2        =3Dca'e        x1 se cmima ro lo me x2 me'u e no lo na=
=20
me x2

If we accept this definition, a set referred to by=20
{lo'i/le'i/la'i}-sumti consists of only the referent of {lo/le/la [PA]=20
broda} or {lo/le/la PA sumti}. Contrastively, if we define it as=20
{selcmi}=3D{se cmima}, the set may include what is/are other than the=20
referent of {lo/le/la [PA] broda} or {lo/le/la PA sumti}. It is not yet=20
officially determined which interpretation is to be accepted.//



As far as I know, gunma2 and cmima1 are non-exhaustive, in other words=20
they do not necessarily show all the members of gunma1 and cmima2=20
respectively. (Correct me if I'm wrong!)

I don't like very much the idea of using the sel- rafsi in a=20
non-compositional way, for making lujvo of the form {selbroda} whose=20
meaning cannot be derived from {se broda}. It seems there's a pretty=20
wide implicit agreement that the sel/ter/vel/xel rafsi should be regular=20
(semantically compositional).

So, I think the BPFK should make an official decision on whether {loi=20
broda}/{lo'i broda} might include things that do not broda among their=20
referents, and clarify the formal definitions accordingly if necessary.

I would expect them to never include things that do not broda. If so,=20
the definition should probably be modified as shown below:

=E2=80=A2 loi [PA] broda  =3D  lo gunma be lo [PA] broda .e no drata be ri
=E2=80=A2 lo'i [PA] broda  =3D  lo se cmima be lo [PA] broda .e no drata be=
 ri

What do you think?

mu'o mi'e la .ilmen.


